#! ia 1.0

@capability host-lower
  meaning
    says "Lower a Claude, Codex or Grok plugin into a new kit workspace with ia init --from: every file and frontmatter key gets one disposition in the lowering map, and any unresolved construct refuses the whole lowering."
    answers "How does an existing plugin become IA records without losing anything?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook host-lower]
    checks [@check host-validate]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability host-project
  meaning
    says "Render a lowered workspace back into a plugin with ia project --product plugin, into an absent or empty directory, and prove the round trip with --check --compare against the original: content-exact needs --check --compare, and the check also reports whether lowering the output again is a fixed point."
    answers "How is a plugin rendered from records and shown to be lossless?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook host-project]
    checks [@check host-fixed-point]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]

@capability host-evaluate
  meaning
    says "Measure whether a model-invocable skill triggers when it should and not when it should not: ten and ten prompts as cases of a contract requirement, a run manifest with a session cap first, the original and the regenerated plugin side by side in the logged-in host config."
    answers "Does this skill trigger correctly, and is the regenerated plugin no worse?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook host-evaluate]
    checks [@check host-trigger-eval]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write, external-write]

@capability host-qualify
  meaning
    says "Qualify a plugin on its hosts: isolated install, strict validation, component inventory and listing cost, and the Codex host smoke, recording each observation as evidence for a host-feature row."
    answers "Does this plugin load on its hosts, and at what cost?"
  composition
    playbooks [@playbook host-qualify]
  execution
    effects [read, local-write]
